# OQ-8, L §8.2 `pinned:`: "The pins one def forms under many as if (a known d at each of its keys, as cpi_yy[m] as if
# {known d}) print once, their days merged into maximal spans". first_seen[d] reads n as known on d: 1 on
# 2026-03-01, 2 from v2's known 2026-03-02 (L §5.11 as if `known D`: the cut K inside), so tot = 1 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 7; the
# four pins print once, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-03 and 2026-03-10 (the layout of the merged line is refcore's).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input n: int
input a: date
input b: date
input c: date
def first_seen[d in days]: int = n as if {known d} at reader
def tot: int = sum(first_seen[d] for d in days where d >= a and d <= b) + first_seen[c] at reader

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 1
  a = 2026-03-01
  b = 2026-03-03
  c = 2026-03-10

version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-03-02
  replace n = 2

ask q1: tot law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: 7
  pinned: known d = 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-03, 2026-03-10
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
